      "answer": "Yes. At a fintech internship I owned an A/B test on the signup form. Hypothesis was that removing the phone number field would raise completion. I computed sample size beforehand, about 6,000 users per arm for a two-point lift at 80 percent power. I ran it for twelve days. Completion went from 61.3 to 64.8 percent, significant at p under 0.01. But I also checked downstream fraud flags, which rose slightly, so I recommended making phone optional rather than removing it. Product went with that.",
