      "answer": "For my capstone, a study-group app, I had to pick between polling and WebSockets for chat. Polling every 3 seconds was trivial on our Heroku setup but would have meant about 20 requests a minute per user. WebSockets needed sticky sessions, which our free tier didn't support well. I picked long polling as a middle ground. It cut requests by around 80% in my load test with 50 simulated users, and I documented that we'd move to WebSockets if we paid for a real host.",
